    },
    {
      "id": "9b3e1ec0-c8f0-4259-b373-1b8840adab88",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "blue",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left",
        "level": 2,
        "isToggleable": false
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "What is a feature spec?",
          "styles": {}
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "9d015d24-823d-40da-bd50-8d14a0f1d536",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "default",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The feature spec is a document that is a walk-through of your project from the users perspective. It provides a listing of all the features you are envisioning for the product. The feature spec functions as your overall plan for the project. Rather than thinking about it as locking you in, this is an opportunity to think through your product in detail. Think of it as a living document, don’t be afraid to change it later as your ideas about the project mature. It does not need to be an exhaustive document. Joel Spolsky (of Stackoverflow and more recently Trello) has a nice writeup of the why and how of specs here: ",
          "styles": {}
        },
        {
          "type": "link",
          "href": "http://www.joelonsoftware.com/articles/fog0000000035.html",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "joelonsoftware",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " and here’s some great general ",
          "styles": {}
        },
        {
          "type": "link",
          "href": "https://medium.com/dali-lab/9-ideas-for-more-useful-feature-specs-7ca5c679ca3c",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "tips on feature specs",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ".",
          "styles": {}
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "8a154b0f-ec00-4762-b658-fd96f52e4093",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "default",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "However",
          "styles": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", for our needs — the feature spec will be much simpler: a listing of what you think you need to build this term to be able to prove out your idea.",
          "styles": {}
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "edae7b41-6743-4631-81ae-9bcc950447a5",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "default",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left"
      },
      "content": [],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "2745bd41-fff7-41e2-aa07-4efa4f307ee0",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "blue",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left",
        "level": 2,
        "isToggleable": false
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Another document?",
          "styles": {}
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "2624c228-b56f-402f-9368-260490042c16",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "default",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Nope!",
          "styles": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " ",
          "styles": {}
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "78f8830e-b6bc-4f12-be2e-8ad7f0da5db5",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "default",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Rather than creating a separate document for this — we’re going to use GitHub Projects Roadmaps (beta)!  Read more about it here: ",
          "styles": {}
        },
        {
          "type": "link",
          "href": "https://github.blog/changelog/2023-01-31-roadmap-in-projects-public-beta/",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "https://github.blog/changelog/2023-01-31-roadmap-in-projects-public-beta/",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " ",
          "styles": {}
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "06d26c13-2bff-4899-b6a7-0a012cba48cb",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "default",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "link",
          "href": "https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/101840513/215614784-d38e2c40-5dca-4ab7-9724-49e5b73f3c9b.mp4?_=2",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/101840513/215614784-d38e2c40-5dca-4ab7-9724-49e5b73f3c9b.mp4?_=2",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "f63322f3-fe53-42db-b00b-6104bc15e1af",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "default",
        "textColor": "default",
